{102}{}{Not now. Not with bullets in the air.}

# New Reno: The Silver Garter
{110}{}{Stairs down to the old hotel's service entrance.}
{111}{}{The Silver Garter. Half the neon sign still flickers above the boarded front. The servants' stairs at the side lead down into the old hotel.}

# Redding: The Slag
{120}{}{Stairs down into an old ore tunnel.}
{121}{}{Behind the sheds a stairway leads down into a shaft nobody has worked in years. Somebody has swept the steps.}

# Vault City: The Cesspit
{130}{}{Cellar stairs behind the boarding house.}
{131}{}{Clean steps, a clean railing. The boarding house looks respectable. What's under it doesn't.}

# NCR: The Trough
{140}{}{Stairs down, with a stenciled number above them: 9.}
{141}{}{Licensed Establishment No. 9 of the Republic, says the stencil. The drovers just call it the Trough.}

# San Francisco: The Bilge
{150}{}{Stairs down into the half-flooded ferry terminal.}
{151}{}{Rusted stairs lead down into the old ferry terminal. It smells of salt, rot and cheap perfume.}
